&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cost of 2 Pens and 3 eraser = Rs. 34&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cost of 3 pens and 4 eraser = Rs. 49&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let the cost of a pen be Rs. x and the cost of an eraser be Rs y.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;According to problem,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; 2x + 3y = 34&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; 8x + 12y = 136&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; ----(1)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;According to problem,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; 3x + 4y = 49&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; 9x + 12y = 147&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; ----(2)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;From (2) &amp;ndash; (1) we get,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; x = 147 &amp;ndash; 136 = 11&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cost of 2 pens = Rs. (2 &amp;times; 11)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;Rs. 22&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;there4; The cost of 2 pens is Rs. 22&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

