en.value:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Three speeds = 5 km/h, 8 km/h and 10 km/h&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Formula used&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Time = Distance/Speed; 1 hour = 60 minutes&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;let the distance travelled in each speed &amp;nbsp;is x km&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Time taken in each speed by a person to travel same disatnce = x/5; x/8 and x/10&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;According to question&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(x/5) + (x/8) + (x/10) = 2 + (33/60)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; (8x + 5x + 4x)/40 = 2 + (11/20)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr; 17x/40 = (40 + 11)/20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;17x/40 = 51/20&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;x = (51&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 40)/(17&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 20)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;x = 6&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Total distance travelled in three different speed = 6 + 6 + 6&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;18 km&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;there4; Total distance travelled by a person is 18 km&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

