&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The LCM of two numbers = 60&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The ratio of two numbers = 4 : 5&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Concept Used:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A ratio indicates how many times one number contains another.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The ratio of the two numbers is 4 : 5&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LCM of the two numbers = 60&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; 4&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(\times\)&lt;/span&gt; 5&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(\times\)&lt;/span&gt; a = 60&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;a = 3&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The number is:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;1st number = 4a = 4 &amp;times; 3 = 12&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;2nd number = 5a = 5 &amp;times; 3 = 15&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;The sum of two number = 1st number + 2nd number = 12 &lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; 15 = 27&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;there4; The sum of the two numbers is 27.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

